abstract: >
  Lean 4 and SymPy formalization project for the information geometry of
  quantum gravity, featuring a maintained representation-depth theorem spine
  spanning projective geometry (PGA), operator algebras, and thermodynamic
  inference. The repository identifies a stable core centered on modular and
  spectral operator theory, Krein-Clifford doubled geometry, and
  Drazin/inverse-kernel anomaly analysis with Einstein-source bridges.

  Recent architectural extensions formalize the holographic boundary of
  Conformal Cyclic Cosmology (CCC) via Cuntz-Toeplitz noncommutative
  quasicrystals (Penrose tilings), where matter-field sockets are modeled by
  Golden Ratio q-deformed Canonical Commutation Relations (q-CCR). The framework
  links the E_{7(7)} Freudenthal black-hole entropy invariant (J_4) to scalar
  microscopic entropy anchors on the fractal boundary. It also institutes an
  information-geometric UV cutoff: the self-concordant Massieu-Planck vacuum
  flow, measured by the Itakura-Saito divergence, terminates at a positive
  minimal phase-space pixel bounded by the Cramer-Rao information metric.

  The workflow couples hypothesis-first black-book research with theorem-target
  promotion. Directed by human architectural vision and executed in open
  collaboration with AI coding agents, the codebase is secured under Lean-native
  architecture audits, DAG diagnostics, SymPy witnesses, theorem-honesty
  sockets, and strict zero-debt vacuity checks.
